      {
        "id": 52666,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-01-28T11:55:44.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think about the only time when you can use a multi-target effect on the same target twice is the Adept's Scherzo of Frost and Flame song, which basically says \"Hit one target for one point of fire damage. Hit one target for one point of cold damage.\" - it doesn't specify that the targets need to be different so in this case you can hit the same thing twice if you want.</p><p>But yes, I like being able to squeeze extra damage (or, in Ab'Zero's case, a free heal) out of a multi-target attack by hitting a fellow hero. Mr Fixer (with Driving Mantis out) as mentioned, or Nightmist with her Amulet, or Ab'Zero when he has both modules out and you whack him with fire damage (obviously you're likely to be playing Ra when you do this) so he can then either heal or hit someone else with cold damage :).</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:26:37.825Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
